Reference binary
----------------
Stock aw882xx_dlkm.ko from amethyst OS3.0.306.0 (vendor_dlkm), which links
FourSemi v4.0.7 (20230609). It was only read (symbols, relocations,
strings, disassembly) to find where v4.0.9.3 differs from what the device
shipped. Nothing from it is copied.

Local changes (all marked "amethyst:" in the source)
----------------------------------------------------
fsm-dev.h
  - Feature set of the stock module: CONFIG_FSM_MISC, CODEC, FIRMWARE, I2C.
    CONFIG_FSM_SYSFS and CONFIG_FSM_MTK turned off (CONFIG_FSM_Q6AFE was
    already off).
  - struct fsm_config: new uint16_t ramp_volume after amb_tempr (stock has
    it there, offset 0x1a), for FSM_Ramp_Volume.

fsm_public.h
  - Prototypes for fsm_set_ramp_volume() and fsm_log_exception(), and the
    three Xiaomi exception event ids stock uses.

fsm_core.c
  - g_fsm_config.ramp_volume starts at 0, as in stock.
  - fsm_config_vol(): stock v4.0.7 behaviour. A device at position LTOP or
    LBTM takes cfg->ramp_volume, the others cfg->volume. Only the 8-bit
    volume field (bits 15:8 of 0x16 on FS19xx, of 0x06 otherwise) is
    written, through fsm_set_bf() (read-modify-write). v4.0.9.3 wrote the
    whole register as (volume << 8) | 0xC0 from cfg->volume for every
    device.
  - New fsm_set_ramp_volume(), rebuilt from stock (see below).

fs1958.c
  - g_fs19xx_pll_tbl, 12.288 MHz BCLK: 0xA2 = 0x02A0, 0xA3 = 0x0018 as in
    stock (v4.0.9.3: 0x0540, 0x0030).
  - fs19xx_i2c_reset(): read PWRCTRL back once after the 0x0002 write, as
    stock does.
  - fs19xx_reg_init(): no fs19xx_read_dtype() (not in stock; its result was
    unused). The function is removed.
  - fs19xx_pre_calib(): stock version. No power-down/up around the changes
    and no noise-gate (0x39) write.
  - fs19xx_start_up(): log "PA data exception" when start-up fails (stock
    reports it to miev).

fsm_codec.c
  - The re25 workqueue (fsm_set_re25_work and friends) is removed. It only
    called fsm_afe_mod_ctrl(), which is a constant 0 without q6afe/IPI;
    stock has none.
  - fsm_codec_register(): call the machine driver's set_smartpa_codec()
    (commented out upstream, called by stock) and log "PA detection
    exception" when the component cannot be registered.
  - fsm_spksw_gpio_put(): stock behaviour, including the volume 0 / 50 ms /
    volume 255 sequence around the switch while ultrasound is on.
  - New FSM_Ramp_Volume control (0..255, SND_SOC_NOPM), with
    fsm_ramp_volume_get/put as in stock.

fsm_i2c.c
  - Drop the #includes of fsm_class.c, fsm_q6afe.c, fsm_mtk_ipi.c and the
    MediaTek speaker-type header, and the mtk_spk_set_type() call.
  - Declare the machine driver's check_smartpa_type()/set_smartpa_type().
  - DT names as in stock and in the amethyst DT: "spksw-gpio" (upstream:
    "spk-sw-gpio"); the IRQ line is looked up under "interrupts" like stock
    (upstream: "irq-gpio"). The amethyst nodes have no such property, so the
    IRQ line stays unclaimed, exactly as in stock. The chip interrupt is
    unused in both: fsm_detect_device() clears use_irq.
  - fsm_log_exception() replaces stock's fs_mievent_report(): it logs the
    event instead of sending it to miev, so aw882xx_dlkm does not depend on
    miev. Called for "PA i2c exception" when the device is not detected.

fsm_misc.c
  - Declare re25_data only when q6afe/IPI is built (unused-variable error
    otherwise).

FSM_Ramp_Volume reconstruction
------------------------------
The control is in stock but not in any source found. Stock disassembly:

  fsm_ramp_volume_get: value[0] = g_fsm_config.ramp_volume; pr_info; 0.
  fsm_ramp_volume_put: pr_info; fsm_set_ramp_volume(value[0]); return 0.
  fsm_set_ramp_volume(v):
    lock g_fsm_mutex
    if ((unsigned)v > 255) { pr_debug "invalid volume"; v = 255; }
    g_fsm_config.ramp_volume = v
    if (!stream_muted):
      first device on fsm_dev_list with pos_mask & 0xC (LTOP|LBTM)
        -> the inlined body of fsm_config_vol() for it, i.e.
           fsm_set_bf(dev, is19xx ? 0x7816 : 0x7806, v)
      none (or dev_count == 0) -> pr_err "Failed to set ramp volume,
        NO RCV/Left PA"
    unlock
  kcontrol: "FSM_Ramp_Volume", snd_soc_info_volsw, min 0, max 255,
  reg/rreg SND_SOC_NOPM, shift 0, no invert.

There is no ramp, step or delay in the kernel. On amethyst the device at
position 0x8 (LTOP) is the amplifier at 0x34 (fs19xx.fsm), i.e. the top
speaker that also drives the earpiece.
